{#
    Rows for the gutter grid. Every list on the site that puts a short fact in
    the left column and an entry in the right one is built from these, so the
    titles line up down the page whatever the gutter happens to carry.

    `entryRow` is the two-line form: a title with a summary under it, used by
    the working and reading sections. `href` is optional — the work list passes
    none, so a role renders as plain text rather than as a link to nowhere.
    `quietGutter` keeps the gutter's text in the accessibility tree while
    taking it out of the visual column; see the work list for why.

    `postRow` is the one-line form: a date in the gutter and a linked title.
    The date arrives already formatted, because the archives want the day and
    the home page has 96px to spend.
#}
{% macro entryRow(gutter, title, summary = null, href = null, quietGutter = false) %}
<li class="gutter-grid__row">
    <span class="gutter-grid__gutter gutter-grid__gutter--strong{% if quietGutter %} gutter-grid__gutter--quiet{% endif %}">{{ gutter }}</span>
    <span class="gutter-grid__entry">
        <span class="gutter-grid__title">{% if href %}<a href="{{ href }}">{{ title }}</a>{% else %}{{ title }}{% endif %}</span>
        {%- if summary %}
        <span class="gutter-grid__summary">{{ summary }}</span>
        {%- endif %}
    </span>
</li>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro postRow(item, date) %}
<li class="gutter-grid__row">
    <time class="gutter-grid__gutter" datetime="{{ item.date | w3Date }}">{{ date }}</time>
    <span class="gutter-grid__title"><a href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.data.title }}</a></span>
</li>
{% endmacro %}
